    description: Archived release of this repository
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/AD-Assurance-Lab/formal-verification--steering--code
url: >-
  https://huggingface.co/datasets/AD-Assurance-Lab/steering-verification-captures
abstract: >-
  Two small end-to-end steering networks are trained per road in the
  CARLA simulator, one on clear weather alone and one on four
  conditions, and each is distilled to a size that can be verified.
  Bound propagation then reads the weights and biases to compute how
  far the steering can drift at every weather strength between two
  captured images, without driving. Under fog and under low sun a
  network whose steering error at the captured condition sits well
  inside safe limits leaves its lane on every lap, and its worst case
  lies in between the conditions a test campaign would drive.
keywords:
  - formal verification
  - autonomous driving
  - neural network verification
  - CARLA
  - robustness
  - operational design domain
